[\"date\"],\n","    ghana[\"cases_ma7\"]\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Seven-Day Moving Average of COVID-19 Cases\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Date\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Average Cases\")\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"Z_RYBoV2kdog","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787051523084,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":878,"user":{"displayName":"Clement Kofi Okyere Biew","userId":"06693515639474326220"}},"outputId":"0dd2186f-7189-4d90-e241-694a8d5f3355"},"execution_count":10,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Seven-Day Moving Average of Deaths"],"metadata":{"id":"kxrVuKVVkn5c"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["ghana[\"deaths_ma7\"] = (\n","    ghana[\"new_deaths\"]\n","    .rolling(window=7)\n","    .mean()\n",")"],"metadata":{"id":"8TTojNwnkjXp","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787051558333,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":101,"user":{"displayName":"Clement Kofi Okyere Biew","userId":"06693515639474326220"}}},"execution_count":11,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["plt.figure(figsize=(14,6))\n","\n","plt.plot(\n","    ghana[\"date\"],\n","    ghana[\"deaths_ma7\"]\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Seven-Day Moving Average of COVID-19 Deaths\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Date\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Average Deaths\")\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"BHsYNHPoksI1","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787051594451,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":718,"user":{"displayName":"Clement Kofi Okyere Biew","userId":"06693515639474326220"}},"outputId":"6178303b-201f-4a27-896c-fba80a004ea8"},"execution_count":12,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Seven-Day Moving Average of Deaths\n","\n","The seven-day moving average of daily deaths reveals a clearer mortality trend than the raw daily death counts.\n","\n","Average daily deaths remained relatively low during the early stages of the outbreak before increasing during June and July. Elevated mortality levels persisted through portions of August before declining towards the end of the study period.\n","\n","The smoothed death trend generally follows the broader pattern observed in reported cases, although the magnitude of change is substantially smaller."],"metadata":{"id":"cJufPEGfneLi"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Interpretation of Results\n","\n","## Daily Reported Cases\n","\n","The daily reported COVID-19 cases in Ghana exhibited substantial variability throughout the study period.\n","\n","Reported case counts remained relatively low during March and April 2020 before increasing noticeably from May onwards. Several sharp spikes were observed between June and August, indicating periods of intensified transmission or reporting activity.\n","\n","The highest reported daily case count exceeded 1,500 cases during the study period.\n","\n","The presence of large fluctuations suggests that daily case counts alone may not adequately represent the underlying outbreak trend, motivating the use of moving-average techniques.\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Daily Reported Deaths\n","\n","Daily reported deaths were generally low throughout the study period.\n","\n","Many days recorded zero deaths, while occasional spikes were observed during June, July, and August.\n","\n","The highest recorded daily death count was 15 deaths.\n","\n","Compared with reported cases, death counts exhibited lower magnitude but still showed noticeable variability over time.\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Seven-Day Moving Average of Cases\n","\n","The seven-day moving average reveals the underlying trend in reported COVID-19 cases after reducing day-to-day fluctuations.\n","\n","The smoothed trend suggests:\n","\n","- A gradual increase in transmission activity from March through June.\n","- Sustained growth during June and July.\n","- Peak transmission activity occurring around late July to early August.\n","- A decline in average daily cases during August and September.\n","\n","The moving-average curve provides a clearer representation of outbreak dynamics than the raw daily case counts."],"metadata":{"id":"dQXok9o3nxN-"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Distribution of Daily Cases\n","\n","The distribution of reported daily cases is examined to understand the spread and concentration of observations."],"metadata":{"id":"tW1mj3Znk6HD"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n","\n","plt.hist(\n","    ghana[\"new_cases\"],\n","    bins=20\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Distribution of Daily COVID-19 Cases\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Daily Cases\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Frequency\")\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"H9slGqI9k0zx","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787051642360,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":646,"user":{"displayName":"Clement Kofi Okyere Biew","userId":"06693515639474326220"}},"outputId":"af0237ff-58d0-4323-f661-4af5fdf59507"},"execution_count":13,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Distribution of Daily Cases\n","\n","The distribution of daily COVID-19 cases is highly right-skewed.\n","\n","Most observations are concentrated at lower case counts, while a relatively small number of days recorded very large numbers of cases.\n","\n","This pattern is consistent with the descriptive statistics reported earlier, where the mean daily case count exceeded the median daily case count.\n","\n","The presence of several unusually large observations contributes to the long right tail of the distribution."],"metadata":{"id":"tIHFq9TYnPtV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Distribution of Daily Deaths"],"metadata":{"id":"HQrzlEDPlJo8"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n","\n","plt.hist(\n","    ghana[\"new_deaths\"],\n","    bins=15\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Distribution of Daily COVID-19 Deaths\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Daily Deaths\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Frequency\")\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"d4Y0kot9lAho","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787051697950,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":465,"user":{"displayName":"Clement Kofi Okyere Biew","userId":"06693515639474326220"}},"outputId":"5f6a708c-11db-4d0a-925f-eb0150e32712"},"execution_count":14,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Distribution of Daily Deaths\n","\n","The distribution of daily COVID-19 deaths is also right-skewed.\n","\n","Most observations are concentrated near zero deaths, while relatively few days recorded higher mortality counts.\n","\n","This observation is consistent with the descriptive statistics, where the median daily death count was zero and the maximum reported daily death count was fifteen.\n","\n","The distribution suggests that periods of elevated mortality were relatively uncommon during the study period."],"metadata":{"id":"gZ6aUI-1nCxe"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Key Findings\n","\n","Based on the exploratory analysis:\n","\n","- Daily reported COVID-19 cases exhibited substantial variability throughout the study period.\n","- Reported case activity increased from March through July before declining during August and September.\n","- Several periods of elevated case activity were observed between June and August 2020.\n","- The highest reported daily case count exceeded 1,500 cases.\n","- Daily reported deaths were generally low but displayed occasional spikes.\n","- The highest recorded daily death count was 15 deaths.\n","- The seven-day moving average of cases suggests that transmission activity peaked around late July to early August.\n","- The seven-day moving average of deaths indicates elevated mortality during portions of June, July, and August.\n","- The distributions of both daily cases and daily deaths are strongly right-skewed.\n","- A small number of high-case and high-death days contributed disproportionately to overall outbreak activity.\n","\n","The exploratory analysis provides evidence of changing outbreak intensity over time and supports the development of a statistical surveillance framework in subsequent stages of the project."],"metadata":{"id":"ax2tWOcWm9LB"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"TT4tJDWulOKk"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}